For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

GADGETRY: appliances collectively.
GATEWAY: an entrance that can be closed by a gate.
GEOMETRY: the pure mathematics of points and lines and curves and surfaces.
GRADIENT: a graded change in the magnitude of some physical quantity or dimension.
GRAPH: a visual representation of the relations between certain quantities, represented as points, plotted with reference to a set of axes.
GRAVITY: (physics) the force of attraction between all masses in the universe.
